  - Safety: Extract and compare grade 3/4 AEs, neutropenia rates between arms.
- Synthesis:
  - As only one eligible RCT is expected, narrative synthesis will be primary; no meta-analysis unless more trials are 
identified.
  - Assess risk of bias (randomization, allocation concealment, blinding, incomplete outcome data, selective reporting, 
early stopping).
  - Applicability to infants of HIV-infected mothers: Identify evidence gap if no eligible RCTs in that subgroup.
- Interpretation:
  - Weigh mortality benefit versus safety signals (notably neutropenia).
  - Consider implications in settings with high bacterial resistance (noted in Study 1 background) and limited ART 
access.


